     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi<div><br></div><div>I think there is a bug with hypergeometric_rng function (or at least with its documentation)</div><div><br></div><div>I have this stan file:</div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>generated quantities</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>  n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hypergeometric_rng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">80</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>When I run it from R I see this:</div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:14.5455px;font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:14.5455px;font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span>sm &lt;- stan_model(file=&quot;ttt.stan&quot;)</span></font></pre></pre><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:14.5455px;font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">&gt; </span>res &lt;- sampling(sm,data=data,iter=1, chains=1, algorithm=&quot;Fixed_param&quot;)<br></font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>SAMPLING FOR MODEL </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;ttt&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> NOW </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">CHAIN </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">).</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Error : Exception thrown at line 7: Error in function boost::math::cdf(const hypergeometric_distribution&lt;double&gt;&amp;, const double&amp;): Random variable out of range: must be less than both n and r but got 40&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">error occurred during calling the sampler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sampling </span><span style=\"color:#008\">not</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">done</span></span></pre></div></code></div><br>Stan documentation (2.9.0) says:</div><div><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">int hypergeometric_rng(int N, real a, real b)<br></font>Generate a hypergeometric variate with N trials, total success count of a, and<br>total failure count of b; may only be used in generated quantities block</blockquote><div><br></div><div>Seems to me that so long as N&lt;=a+b there shouldn&#39;t be a problem. So what&#39;s wrong?</div><div><br></div><div>Another issue: </div><div>If I change the sampling line to:</div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hypergeometric_rng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">80.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">20.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>I get a compiler error:</div></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:14.5455px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">SYNTAX ERROR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> MESSAGE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FROM PARSER</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#606\">No</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> matches </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">  hypergeometric_rng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#606\">Available</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> argument signatures </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> hypergeometric_rng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">  hypergeometric_rng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></span></pre></div></code></div><br>so obviously, the documentation is wrong regarding input types.</div><div><br></div><div>yet another issue: in general, to use this function I need to covert  real values (parameters) to ints. Why is there not real to int conversion? </div><div><br></div><div>If the problem is simply wrong documentation, I&#39;d like to know the correct usage so that I can work around this.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks !</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
